  "worked_solution": "The complement of $C,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{C},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $C.$ To represent $\\overset{\u2015}{C},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $C,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/9ff9378b08cdd6175901e40a70c3a6ed38cfa21cd15e948f766f1a668345834a.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $\u25fb,$ and $\u2663.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $C.$ Therefore, the complement of $C$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{C}={\u25fb,\u2663}.\n$$",
